  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-70122",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We replace $m$ with $4$ and $n$ with $1$ in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2m}{n+4}-\\frac{m-2}{2n} & = \\\\ \\frac{2(4)}{1+4}-\\frac{4-2}{2(1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{2}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{5}-1 & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{5}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{8-5}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
